[Music]  okay  so this is my review of episode four of  wanda vision we interrupt this program  so first off  i was mostly impressed with the first  three episodes the amount of detail put  into it the amount of effort put into it  how unique it is but i did feel like it  was struggling with the amount of main  plot they were pushing along  and only giving you a little bit each  episode to keep the story going forward  but that all changes here in this  episode this episode to me  was spectacular in so many different  ways i think it's the  best episode i could have just imagined  getting for an episode for after  what those first three episodes set up  and why this episode's so effective  is it sets out a lot of things for where  the season is gonna go now and get you  really now excited because you're now  actually realizing the protagonist of  this story actually isn't wanda  she actually is the antagonist in this  story  your protagonist is gonna be monica  rambo and what's so  awesome about this episode is it flips  perspective for you  because you're seeing everything that  happened in the beginning now from the  outsiders perspective  which i always think works and is really  effective and interesting but it also  really works because you see the  characters coming back and out from the  mcu of darcy lewis  jimmy wu is that those two characters  are  taking the role of the audience here  they're  just as confused as we are they're  trying to figure it out and it's perfect  to put  us in their place and really enjoy their  scenes even just seeing jimmy woo  trying to figure it out on the  whiteboard who everybody is it's exactly  what we're all doing him writing his  vision alive  yada yada it's the same stuff that  you're seeing in all the easter egg  videos  and what you're reading on reddit that  is what they're doing and it was smart  they made characters like that for us to  kind of  be in the driver's seat for us as an  audience now let me elaborate on what  i'm saying about  monochrombo being the protagonist and  wanda being the antagonist which i think  obviously makes this already something  mcu is so good at is just  doing something unique and creative in  their own universe  always changing things up and it shows  the again  amazing effects that infinity war and  the snap  had on the mcu and took it to the next  level where i started  really appreciating it for going into  different  places and now to show that they can  have  the reactions to people coming back from  the snap from all different areas  was so effective and especially in this  opening that played like a horror  sequence  with monica coming back we learned that  she was literally gone for five years  that her mother from captain marvel  maria rambo passed away  three years ago while she was gone  already for two years so  the effects of that it was just crazy to  see this hospital filling in they didn't  have enough room  but it already gets you to sympathize  with monica rambo and then  this episode plays out well with her  character to see how she got trapped  in wanda's world but it's also showing  you that  where she works the sword headquarters  and now they set up camp here  outside of this missing town of west  view is that  they're the ones we're with trying to  figure out what is  wanda doing and why it works so well to  have wanda play the antagonist role  right now is because it works so well  thematically with the grief she is  feeling about vision's death  and the denial she's in and not  accepting it and  making obviously this fake reality now  this sitcom world i saw  a great theory that the youtube channel  screen crush had  does great easter egg videos about the  show but him  saying that wanda's just creating  this sitcom world that she imagined of  just what a happy life in america is  like from growing up and watching it as  a kid  i know that was so fascinating and i'm  completely in that theory and believe it  that  wanda's created this false reality to  escape from what really happened to  vision  and i thought it was also interesting  that agnes the nosy neighbor played by  catherine hahn  i am so down to theory that she is also  a witch from the comics and was probably  someone that confided  in wanda when wanda was going through  this grief and led her down this path  and clearly wants wanted to have  children for some reason but with all  this great mystery the show's already  had you're already getting so many  payoffs here because you're getting  answers already you're getting  to see monaco is the one who sent in  that drone you're seeing the man who  came through the sewer and i love the  connection they had  with them watching on the tv and how  that came about and  bringing in that great humor with darcy  enjoying the sitcom i even loved the  line and she was like oh great monica's  got a speaking part now i thought that  was really good and her  and jimmy worked together comedically  really well and you really again got  that huge payoff from last week because  we got to see now wanda use her scarlet  witch powers  on monica and then get this flash of  vision when he was dead which was  really sad and worked really well and  you really felt for wanda here  but it gives you your motivation of why  she's doing clearly what she's doing  we're going to learn more about how  powerful wanda really is  remember she has all these connections  to the affinity stones she's done  something here where she's created this  world trap these people of this town  this whole town she has in a bubble  and it's just an awesome thing to see  and be  along this ride now and figuring out  what wanda is up to and what happened in  that time after vision died and you see  that's why they end with  monica here when she came out of the  bubble was like it's wanda it's  all wanda now i think that's exaggerated  for us as the audience to be like oh my  god wanda's behind all of it but i  clearly think there's other people  influencing her too to  make this bad choice of putting this  reality and not being in touch with the  world and making others suffer  i'm clearly leaning towards agnes here  the nosy neighbor  that she is a bad influence on wanda  because she probably is also a witch  like from the comics so we'll see though  and i thought it was also interesting  that this episode wu and darcy didn't  notice any of agnes in the footage they  were watching so they're clearly  keeping that at bay somewhere because  that probably would be paid off later on  more to her character they just don't  want to go there yet i thought this  episode was absolutely fantastic because  i think people who weren't digging the  first three  this is gonna draw those people back in  because it's really felt connected to  the mcu  it really was now easier to get and  really understand what's going on they  gave you enough answers to do that so  people who felt completely confused  at least got some more to chew on and  can kind of get their grounding where  they're at and having people to attach  to now  as our fellow audience like i said darcy  and jimmy wu  and now making you be like oh man like  wait a second  wanda really is now in this specific  story our antagonist so  how will they get the wanda we know and  love back  and get her to deal with her grief i  really love what they're doing here  i have to give props to kevin feige  because it shows the effect of having a  producer who's  overseeing all this stuff in the mcu but  he's a rare case where he actually still  cares and gives a hundred percent effort  to make sure  it all makes sense it's all smooth and  it has constant quality and that they're  doing something different  and they're doing it again here i love  it's in tv format because tv format is  my favorite as you know but to see the  mcu now take a stab at it  it's really exciting and so far i think  they're crushing it but for me  this episode is the best one yet clearly  9.8 i'm so excited for where this is  gonna go  i was on the edge of my seat this whole  episode and i love that it's based in  mystery and with a great theme of grief  with wanda  so let me know what you thought of it  down below i'd love to hear your  thoughts i read every comment try to  respond as many as i can  please make sure to subscribe i'll be  reviewing every episode of wanda vision  the day  they come out so you don't want to miss  any of those if you like what i do here  i really appreciate a two dollar monthly  donation i have a paypal link down below  that will help me cover more shows and  movies for you guys and i also do  celebrity interviews so  again it will give me what i need to do  this full time  and please follow me at steve varley  show on twitter instagram for more of me  and i'll see you next time

